Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: match textureLoad on a whole identifier, not a prefix

The read-only-storage-to-sampled conversion adds a mip-level argument to
textureLoad calls on the variable it just converted, by searching for:

  "textureLoad(" + info.var_name

That is a prefix match. Godot's SDFGI preprocess shader declares both

  uimage3D src_light;
  uimage3D src_light_aniso;

so the search for src_light also matched src_light_aniso, which then received a
second mip argument when its own turn came around:

  textureLoad(src_light,       pos, 0)     // correct
  textureLoad(src_light_aniso, pos, 0, 0)  // four arguments

  no matching call to 'textureLoad(texture_3d<u32>, vec3<i32>, abstract-int, abstract-int)'

which invalidated SdfgiPreprocessShaderRD variant 8.

The fix is an identifier-boundary test rather than a longer-names-first
ordering: a rewrite for binding x may only touch a textureLoad whose first
argument is exactly the identifier x. Anchoring on a trailing comma would also
have worked against Tint's current formatting, but the rule being enforced is
"whole identifier", so that is what the code now says. Applied at both the
shadow-texture and direct-variable sites, which shared the hazard.

Measured on a Tesla P40 through Chrome/WebGPU, Chariot on Forward+:

  SDFGI WGSL parse failures   1 -> 0
  cascading invalid-module    1 -> 0
  GPUValidationError         14 -> 6   (with 0025)

diff --git a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
--- a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
@@ -175,6 +175,19 @@
 // buffer must never be rewritten to read-only: the result is a module that does
 // not parse. Resolving the declared type rather than trusting Tint's
 // "_atomic" name suffix keeps this correct if Tint's naming ever changes.
+// True when position p_at in p_wgsl is NOT inside an identifier -- i.e. the
+// identifier that ended just before it really ended there. Used so a rewrite for
+// one texture variable cannot reach into a longer name that starts the same way.
+static bool _wgsl_identifier_ends_at(const String &p_wgsl, int64_t p_at) {
+	if (p_at >= p_wgsl.length()) {
+		return true;
+	}
+	const char32_t c = p_wgsl[p_at];
+	const bool is_identifier_char =
+			(c >= U'a' && c <= U'z') || (c >= U'A' && c <= U'Z') || (c >= U'0' && c <= U'9') || c == U'_';
+	return !is_identifier_char;
+}
+
 static bool _wgsl_storage_decl_has_atomic(const char *p_wgsl, const char *p_decl) {
 	const char *colon = strchr(p_decl, ':');
 	if (!colon) {
@@ -3727,6 +3740,14 @@
 						String search = "textureLoad(" + shadow_name;
 						int64_t pos = 0;
 						while ((pos = ws.find(search, pos)) != -1) {
+							// "textureLoad(src_light" is a PREFIX of "textureLoad(src_light_aniso".
+							// Without a boundary test the mip argument is inserted into the
+							// longer name once for each variable, producing a four-argument
+							// textureLoad on a texture_3d that WGSL rejects.
+							if (!_wgsl_identifier_ends_at(ws, pos + search.length())) {
+								pos += search.length();
+								continue;
+							}
 							int64_t paren_start = pos + String("textureLoad").length();
 							int depth = 0;
 							int64_t insert_mip = -1;
@@ -3856,6 +3877,14 @@
 						String search = "textureLoad(" + info.var_name;
 						int64_t pos = 0;
 						while ((pos = ws.find(search, pos)) != -1) {
+							// "textureLoad(src_light" is a PREFIX of "textureLoad(src_light_aniso".
+							// Without a boundary test the mip argument is inserted into the
+							// longer name once for each variable, producing a four-argument
+							// textureLoad on a texture_3d that WGSL rejects.
+							if (!_wgsl_identifier_ends_at(ws, pos + search.length())) {
+								pos += search.length();
+								continue;
+							}
 							int64_t paren_start = pos + String("textureLoad").length();
 							int depth = 0;
 							int64_t insert_mip = -1;
